  "articleBody": "Texas weather can be brutal, and hail is a common culprit for roof damage. But when you suspect your roof has been hit, navigating the assessment process can be tricky. Making a few common mistakes can lead to delays, denied claims, or even bigger expenses down the line. We want to help you get it right from the start.\n\nMistake 1: Inspecting only the visibly affected slope — how to avoid it: Hail doesn't just hit one side of your roof. An incomplete assessment misses damage on other slopes, gutters, or collateral structures. A thorough professional will check *all* accessible roof planes and related components.\n\nMistake 2: Confusing age-related wear with event-related damage — how to avoid it: It's easy to mistake old wear and tear for fresh storm damage. An experienced assessor can clearly differentiate between normal aging and specific hail impact, which is crucial for insurance claims.\n\nMistake 3: Failing to document pre-existing conditions — how to avoid it: If your roof had prior issues, it's important to document them. A good assessment notes these conditions, ensuring that only new, storm-related damage is attributed to the recent event.\n\nMistake 4: Omitting interior or collateral damage — how to avoid it: Don't forget to check your attic, ceilings, and even detached structures like sheds or carports. Water intrusion or collateral damage might not be immediately obvious but can be significant.\n\nMistake 5: Using unclear photographs without location context — how to avoid it: If you’re taking your own photos, make sure they are high-resolution, dated, and clearly show the damage *in context*. Professionals use both wide shots and close-ups, making it undeniable where the damage is.\n\nMistake 6: Beginning permanent repairs before documentation is complete — how to avoid it: Resist the urge to start major repairs immediately. Document all damage thoroughly with photos and video (if safe) *before* permanent work begins. This protects your claim and ensures nothing is missed.\n\nWhat to Do Next\n\nIf you suspect hail damage, avoiding these mistakes starts with a professional assessment. Contact Discounted Roofing Co. for an honest and clear roof damage assessment. We’ll help you document everything correctly and guide you through the next steps.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-03"
}